# Normalise line endings.
#
# Development happens on Windows, CI runs on Linux, and the services run in
# Linux containers. Without this, every file touched on Windows shows up as a
# whole-file diff, and shell scripts copied into a container fail with
# "bad interpreter". Store everything as LF in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF even if a tool tries to be helpful.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
# Windows batch files must keep Windows line endings (CRLF), or cmd.exe can
# misread them after a fresh clone.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
